  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Terminalia bellirica」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terminalia_bellirica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1322381681,
      "text": "Terminalia bellirica, known as bahera, beleric or bastard myrobalan, is a large deciduous tree in the family Combretaceae. It is common on the plains and lower hills in South and Southeast Asia, where it is also grown as an avenue tree. The basionym is Myrobalanus bellirica Gaertn.. William Roxburgh transferred M. bellirica to Terminalia as \"T. bellerica (Gaertn.) Roxb.\". This spelling error is now widely used, causing confusion. The correct name is Terminalia bellirica (Gaertn.) Roxb."
    }
  },
